10
00:40:54,545 --> 00:41:00,545
Breakin' (also known as Breakdance in the United Kingdom and Break Street '84 in other regions) is a 1984 American breakdancing-themed musical film directed by
Joel Silberg and written by Charles Parker and Allen DeBevoise based on a story by Parker, DeBevoise and Gerald Scaife about dancer Alysha Williams.

11
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
The film's setting was inspired by a 1983 documentary titled Breakin' 'n' Enterin', set in the
multi-racial hip hop club Radio-Tron, based out of MacArthur Park in Los Angeles.

12
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Many of the artists and dancers from that documentary, including Ice-T (who makes his film debut as a club MC), and
Michael "Boogaloo Shrimp" Chambers, went straight from Breakin' 'n' Enterin' to star in Breakin'.

13
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
The film's soundtrack featured the hits "Breakin'...

14
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
There's No Stopping Us" by Ollie & Jerry, "Freakshow on the Dance Floor" by
The Bar-Kays and the UK Top 20 hit "Body Work" by Hot Streak.

15
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
Breakin' was one of the final Cannon film productions released by MGM/UA.

16
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
After release, MGM and Cannon dissolved their distribution deal, reportedly over the potentially X-rated content in John Derek's film Bolero and
MGM's then-policy of not theatrically releasing X-rated material, forcing Cannon to become an in-house distribution company once again.

17
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
Because of this, Breakin' is considered to be the final
financially profitable film released by Cannon.

18
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
Breakin' was released to theaters on May 4, 1984, and despite receiving
negative reviews from critics, it was a box office success.

19
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
A theatrical sequel entitled Breakin' 2: Electric
Boogaloo was released later in the same year.

20
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film explores themes of dancing, rap music,
hip-hop, street gang, breakdance.

21
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The tone is emotional.
